132661	132789	132655	132655	his	473	" I might easily deceive you , Minna , and promise you what my soul tells me is an impossibility ; but I am forced to use too much deceit with others , and with you I will use none . I can not be friend to this young man;--there is a natural dislike -- an instinctive aversion -- something like a principle of repulsion in our mutual nature , which makes us odious to each other . Ask himself -- he will tell you he has the same antipathy against me . The obligation he conferred on me was a bridle to my resentment ; but I was so galled by the restraint , that I could have gnawed the curb till my lips were bloody . "
